Common Dockerfile Instructions

FROM
Specifies the base image. All subsequent layers are built on top of this image.
Example: FROM node:18-alpine

WORKDIR
Sets the working directory inside the container. All following commands run relative to this path.
Example: WORKDIR /app

COPY / ADD
Copies files from the host machine into the container filesystem.
Example: COPY app.js .

RUN
Executes commands during image build time (e.g., installing packages). Each RUN creates a new image layer.

EXPOSE
Documents the port the application listens on. It does not publish the port automatically.
Example: EXPOSE 3000

CMD / ENTRYPOINT
Defines the default command that runs when a container starts.
Example: CMD ["node", "app.js"]

Docker Image Lifecycle (Summary)

1. Dockerfile written – defines image instructions

2. Image built – using docker build

3. Container created – using docker run

4. Application running – inside container

5. Container stopped & removed

6. Image removed – cleanup completed
